krs 1
# Yosys's generic synthesis of a lane GHDL wrote as Verilog, as a script Yosys reads a command a line (yosys -s). The
# format is the comment at the head of ptx.krs. The script is synth's own passes, lightened: each opt is opt -fast in
# place of synth's full opt and opt -full, and fsm and share are left out: the cost read is the lane as it is written,
# its state register as the process holds it and each operation its own operator. What the passes give is the netlist
# its cost is read from: the memories memory -nomap infers before the fine stage maps them to flops, the read ports it
# registers ("merging output FF"), the cells stat counts, and the longest path ltp walks ("(length=").
ruleset yosys
toolchain yosys
header read_source

# the Verilog GHDL wrote
form read_source source = read_verilog {source}\n
# the design's hierarchy from its top, its processes as cells, and its arithmetic and memories as coarse cells
form coarse top = hierarchy -check -top {top}\nproc\nopt_expr\nopt_clean\nopt -fast -nodffe -nosdff\nwreduce\npeepopt\nopt_clean\nalumacc\nopt -fast\nmemory -nomap\nopt_clean\n
# the coarse netlist's statistics written quietly to a log, while its memories are still cells
form memories log = tee -q -o {log} stat\n
# the memories mapped to flops, the coarse cells to gates, and the gates to a netlist by abc's fast script, which folds
# the gates' constants itself: no opt runs between the maps
form fine = memory_map\ntechmap\nabc -fast\nopt -fast\n
# the netlist's cells and its longest path, flops cut
form measure = stat\nltp -noff\n
